```text
A. Cciviur.rrv cH’ Ci-cic
II
MEMO
TO:
City Council and Mayor Orr
FROM:
Charles Bloom, AICP, Planning & Development Director
CC:
Alessandra McCoy Fakelman, Assistant City Attorney
SUBJECT:
Cheyenne Frontier Days (CFD) Planned Unit Development
DATE:
March 18, 2019
Please accept the attached stamped ordinance as a substitute ordinance for the Cheyenne
Frontier Days (CFD) Planned Unit Development zone change for the parcel of land that is
proposed for a remote parking lot during the CFD annual event. The land is located north
of W. College Drive and west of Southwest Drive.
The substitute ordinance is proposed by the Assistant City Attorney to remove elements
of the PUD regulations that were unclear, tangential to zoning issues and that would be
difficult or timely to enforce by the City.
Future PUD regulations would be similarly
scrutinized for relevancy with development and/or design standards.
No substantive changes have been incorporated into this substitute ordinance from what
was recommended for approval by the Planning Commission at their March 4, 2019
meeting.
The Applicant has reviewed the revised ordinance and has agreed to all changes. Thank
you.
Planning & Development Department
2101 O’NeiI Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282
Attachment: proposed substitute stamped ordinance
```

